 "section_summary": "This section contains concluding statistical tables and a Kanto regional map from a Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers (SCAP) Civil Information and Education (CIE) Section report on educational institutions in Gumma Prefecture. It also includes State Department charge-out slips, a transmittal despatch from the U.S. Political Adviser in Tokyo forwarding educational reports for Aichi and Tokushima prefectures, and an internal Department memorandum regarding the Japanese Diet resolution nullifying the Imperial Rescript on Education. Finally, it comprises the title matter, introductory administrative guide, provincial summary tables, and initial detailed roster pages of Part 1 (Aichi Prefecture) of SCAP's comprehensive 1948 educational survey.",
 "subfiles": [
  {
   "about": "Concluding statistical roster and reference map of educational institutions in Gumma Prefecture as of April and November 1946.",
   "continues_previous": true,
   "date": "",
   "doc_type": "report",
   "end_page": 361,
   "from": "Education Branch, Research Unit, Analysis and Research Division, Civil Information and Education Section, General Headquarters, Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers",
   "keywords": [
    "Gumma Prefecture",
    "educational institutions",
    "miscellaneous schools",
    "Kanto region",
    "special schools",
    "juvenile correction"
   ],
   "start_page": 356,
   "summary": "This concluding portion of the Gumma Prefecture educational survey lists enrollment and teacher figures for private female miscellaneous schools and institutions under non-educational ministries, including police and railway youth schools. It concludes with an institutional map of the Kanto region indicating prefectural capitals, major urban populations, and higher education facilities.",
